[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-4463"] :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{0+4}-2}{0}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+4}-2)(\\sqrt{x+4}+2)}{x(\\sqrt{x+4}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x+4-4}{x(\\sqrt{x+4}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+4}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{0+4}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-338481/field-1/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "17b52a57-d327-59a4-87f1-8f2c1f94c3ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338481/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "1fc99c1f-75f5-59ab-9047-139852f97b77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338481/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2f5daf8-e978-513a-b567-a86a92f7824d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338481/field-1/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer-field/choices ["q-338481/field-1/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-338481/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338481" :question/id #uuid "92252b75-35d4-5466-b5eb-58457897a6af" :question/math-academy-id "q-338481" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{8-\\sqrt{8x}}{x-8}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to }\\frac{8-\\sqrt{8x}}{x-8} & =\\frac{8-\\sqrt{8(8)}}{8-8}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{8-\\sqrt{8x}}{x-8} & ={lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{(8-\\sqrt{8x})(8+\\sqrt{8x})}{(x-8)(8+\\sqrt{8x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{{8}^{2}-(\\sqrt{8x})^{2}}{(x-8)(8+\\sqrt{8x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{64-8x}{(x-8)(8+\\sqrt{8x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{-8(x-8)}{(x-8)(8+\\sqrt{8x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{-8\\cancel{(x-8)}}{\\cancel{(x-8)}(8+\\sqrt{8x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 8}\\frac{-8}{8+\\sqrt{8x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{8+\\sqrt{8(8)}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{8+8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338481/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338481"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-4468/selection/393522ee4ded7288062e6072c329c38ecb06c9de712f11faf938346737b8d6d5" :answer/id #uuid "97c72a49-54ee-5327-b262-1da182913087" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4468/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "d30fde5e-d206-5202-a26f-acd1fe1edf47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4468/selection/a7643e7c9a6f47b7e23102a9f593aee2dc956fa29938bf5d470303f0587bc3b1" :answer/id #uuid "24508188-12d5-5aa1-9f0e-d360dba65b3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4468/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "5bb6096f-ccc3-5e14-85a3-641e0c545f08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4468/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" :answer/id #uuid "83ba7d0d-e082-55c3-b59b-b9607f7f2668" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4468/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a85e83e9-1e14-5fff-9cf1-d4709bc85d84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4468/selection/393522ee4ded7288062e6072c329c38ecb06c9de712f11faf938346737b8d6d5" :answer-field/choices ["q-4468/selection/393522ee4ded7288062e6072c329c38ecb06c9de712f11faf938346737b8d6d5" "q-4468/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" "q-4468/selection/a7643e7c9a6f47b7e23102a9f593aee2dc956fa29938bf5d470303f0587bc3b1" "q-4468/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" "q-4468/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4468" :question/id #uuid "3ff5a4e0-9857-5121-92cf-e9b6328f9ca8" :question/math-academy-id "q-4468" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-9}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-9} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3+1}-2}{{3}^{2}-9}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-9} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{(x-3)(x+3)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+1}-2)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{(\\sqrt{x+1})}^{2}-{2}^{2}}{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x+1-4}{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{1}{(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(3+3)(\\sqrt{3+1}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-4468/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4468"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338484/field-1/f594cbbb4a66bc41743b074d8df31c04839068c3f93c44ebcfba00b647948a3b" :answer/id #uuid "adfbf7e5-724e-570d-a920-f0b2140fdbf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338484/field-1/393522ee4ded7288062e6072c329c38ecb06c9de712f11faf938346737b8d6d5" :answer/id #uuid "333dc7a9-ef74-53f8-ae90-5e5e7294c3b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338484/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9ce42d7-ba17-543a-ad4c-ba3d8f394931" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338484/field-1/f594cbbb4a66bc41743b074d8df31c04839068c3f93c44ebcfba00b647948a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-338484/field-1/f594cbbb4a66bc41743b074d8df31c04839068c3f93c44ebcfba00b647948a3b" "q-338484/field-1/393522ee4ded7288062e6072c329c38ecb06c9de712f11faf938346737b8d6d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338484" :question/id #uuid "6417b838-8f56-5a40-8b5a-45b5e7ecb695" :question/math-academy-id "q-338484" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-x-6}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-x-6} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3+1}-2}{{3}^{2}-3-6}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}{{x}^{2}-x-6} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+1}-2)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{({x}^{2}-x-6)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+1})^{2}-{2}^{2}}{(x+2)(x-3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x+1)-4}{(x+2)(x-3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{(x+2)(x-3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{1}{(x+2)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(3+2)(\\sqrt{3+1}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-338484/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338484"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-4467/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "23e859d6-7273-5354-bf41-a04a27d7d07f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4467/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" :answer/id #uuid "7148833d-dcfc-556d-98a2-769bb8ee8426" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4467/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "3e41d188-2da4-545b-92dc-0f528eac4be7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4467/selection/5fd45cec95fc45f99550587cbe4d80dda358c751536fdf37920e2dff6de9568a" :answer/id #uuid "f869a21b-2e40-5816-82a8-baeef2ab7329" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4467/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" :answer/id #uuid "b88d5cc7-80ea-5684-ac5b-b552366580ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4467/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "718dc51d-f545-58cd-80c2-cb003c08fff4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4467/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" :answer-field/choices ["q-4467/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-4467/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" "q-4467/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" "q-4467/selection/5fd45cec95fc45f99550587cbe4d80dda358c751536fdf37920e2dff6de9568a" "q-4467/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4467" :question/id #uuid "4d110047-c802-560a-bccf-6cce5aa93b1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-4467" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+5}-\\sqrt{5}}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=0$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+5}-\\sqrt{5}} & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{0+5}-\\sqrt{5}}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+5}-\\sqrt{5}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})}{(\\sqrt{x+5}-\\sqrt{5})(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})}{{(\\sqrt{x+5})}^{2}-{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})}{x+5-5} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5})}{x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\sqrt{x+5}+\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+5}+\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-4467/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4467"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338515/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "df00b693-51c6-5ee8-8e2d-3ad97cd23022" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186264521 :answer-field/choices ["q-338515/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4471/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "a787e181-1b60-5d74-b492-e3026fe1c9b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4471/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "fb042f75-3b70-5bf9-a61f-c4b40effbfbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4471/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "4b1ea518-9637-5a50-8e25-922e5f877d6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4471/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "d3b6802a-8241-5473-88a4-1e17cdf7cf03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4471/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" :answer/id #uuid "868333c8-3e21-5181-af98-43c91f951bd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4471/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a122ba64-39a8-5687-b975-015093c46c45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4471/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-4471/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-4471/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-4471/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-4471/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-4471/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4471" :question/id #uuid "f7758f03-f7d8-5681-80dc-022d1d05b2a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-4471" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x-1}{x-\\sqrt{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=1$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x-1}{x-\\sqrt{x}} & =\\frac{1-1}{1-\\sqrt{1}}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x-1}{x-\\sqrt{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(x+\\sqrt{x})}{(x-\\sqrt{x})(x+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(x+\\sqrt{x})}{{x}^{2}-{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(x+\\sqrt{x})}{{x}^{2}-x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(x+\\sqrt{x})}{x(x-1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x+\\sqrt{x}}{x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{1+\\sqrt{1}}{1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-4471/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4471"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-4464"] :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{x+3}-2}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=1$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{x+3}-2} & =\\frac{1-1}{\\sqrt{1+3}-2}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{x+3}-2} & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(\\sqrt{x+3}+2)}{(\\sqrt{x+3}-2)(\\sqrt{x+3}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(\\sqrt{x+3}+2)}{{(\\sqrt{x+3})}^{2}-{2}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(\\sqrt{x+3}+2)}{x+3-4} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}\\frac{(x-1)(\\sqrt{x+3}+2)}{x-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}(\\sqrt{x+3}+2) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+3}+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-338496/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "83e713a7-3de6-53c4-b9e2-14eed83e7e63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338496/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b39d826d-10a5-561f-a5c0-b456268562a4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338496/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-338496/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338496" :question/id #uuid "cea8ecd3-a2e6-51b4-876e-28c17aeaa239" :question/math-academy-id "q-338496" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=\\frac{1}{4}$ we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}} & =\\frac{(4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-1)}{(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}})}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{4x-1}{2x-\\sqrt{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{(2x-\\sqrt{x})(2x+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{(2x)^{2}-(\\sqrt{x})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{4{x}^{2}-x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{(4x-1)(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{x(4x-1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{\\cancel{(4x-1)}(2x+\\sqrt{x})}{x\\cancel{(4x-1)}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (1/4)}\\frac{2x+\\sqrt{x}}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}})}{(\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338496/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338496"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-74"] :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x - 2\\sqrt{x}} {x - 4} }.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}\\frac{x-2\\sqrt{x}}{x-4} & =\\frac{4-2\\sqrt{4}}{4-4}=\\frac{0}{0},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x - 2\\sqrt{x}} {x - 4} &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {(x -2 \\sqrt{x})(x+2\\sqrt x)} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n            &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x^2-\\left(2\\sqrt{x}\\right)^2} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x^2-4x} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x(x-4)} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x} {x+2\\sqrt x} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {4} {4+2\\sqrt4} \\\n\t    &=\\dfrac 1 2.\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-75"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac {3x} {\\sqrt{x +1} -1}  }.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=0$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{x+1}-1} & =\\frac{3\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{0+1}-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac {3x} {\\sqrt{x + 1} - 1} \n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(3x)(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{x + 1} - 1)(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{\\left(\\sqrt{x+1}\\right)^2-1^2}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{x+1-1}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{x}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}3(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)\\\n&=3(\\sqrt{0+1}+1)\\\n\t&=6.\n}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
